{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1493051152,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEwNTUxMDUxNTY="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1493206909,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEwNTg0MjYzMDk="},"added":["WIP"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1493208268,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5NzM4MjAyNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1474#issuecomment-297382027"},"message":"So this is a compound issue. First the error message is misleading, as our internal call to clone is already happening with values that should not be there.\n\nSecond, the submodule is configured with the wrong \"URL\" setting:\n\n````\n% cat .gitmodules\n[submodule \"src/aligned\"]\n\tpath = src/aligned\n\turl = ./src/aligned\n````\n\nwhich clearly should be \"../aligned\". Digging out where this is coming from.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1493211819,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5NzQwMDIxMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1474#issuecomment-297400211"},"message":"Reason for the misconfiguration is the switch from a custom helper to the `add` command for registering a freshly installed, previously unknown subdataset. While this is all nice in terms of using common code, it presently refuses to acknowledge any information about the source URL. I propose to adjust `add`, which uses `datalad.distribution.utils._install_subds_inplace()`, to use the URL of `origin` (or whatever effectively primary remote) for `.gitmodules`. In case of a freshly clone subdataset (original situation in this issue)  that will be exactly the URL is was cloned from.\n\nThis will also mitigate the identical issue when a submodule is not installed into a dataset via `-d` immediately, but just installed first, and later registered via `add`.","files":null},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1493211941,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MTA1ODU1OTg1OQ=="},"title":"`add` should use meaningful remote URL for registering submodules","was":"`add` should use meaningful remote URL for registering submodules"},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1493250638,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5NzU3Mjc5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1474#issuecomment-297572791"},"message":"sounds logical although somewhat too magical.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1493901723,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEwNjg4NDUxMTk="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1493901723,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTA2ODg0NTEyMA=="},"added":[],"removed":["WIP"]},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1494039948,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTA3MTQ0NzUzNQ=="},"status":2}]}